7. Using Java 16+ pattern matching, rewrite:
Object obj = getShape();
if (obj instanceof Rectangle) {
    Rectangle r = (Rectangle) obj;
    System.out.println(r.getWidth() * r.getHeight());
} else if (obj instanceof Circle) {
    Circle c = (Circle) obj;
    System.out.println(Math.PI * c.getRadius() * c.getRadius());
}

items.a:
if (obj instanceof Rectangle r) {
    System.out.println(r.getWidth() * r.getHeight());
} else if (obj instanceof Circle c) {
    System.out.println(Math.PI * c.getRadius() * c.getRadius());
} — With Java 16+ pattern matching instanceof, the explicit cast ('Rectangle r = (Rectangle) obj') is eliminated. The binding variable (r, c) is automatically typed and scoped. Eliminates boilerplate, removes redundancy, and the intent is clearer — test and bind happen simultaneously.

